% ADJ52 case-30 — patient observations + queries.
% Same vocabulary as rulebook.adj. Observations ONLY for what THIS patient
% actually has. Tissue histology (PAS/PCR/clonality/AFB) and coeliac serology
% were NOT yet obtained — they are the open uncertainties / candidate next
% steps — so they are deliberately NOT observed.

% --- antecedent seronegative rheumatic picture (preceded GI by ~5 years) ---
observe arthralgia(migratory_preceding_gi)
observe symptom(sicca)
observe symptom(raynaud_like_colour_change)
observe labs(low_titre_ana_ena_negative)
observe treatment_response(arthralgia_settled_on_hydroxychloroquine)

% --- current malabsorptive GI illness ---
observe stool(steatorrhea)
observe weight_loss(severe)

% --- malabsorption / micronutrient derangement (one syndrome) ---
observe labs(low_calcium)
observe labs(low_magnesium)
observe labs(low_phosphate)
observe labs(low_vitamin_d)
observe labs(low_albumin)
observe labs(macrocytic_anaemia)
observe labs(low_bmi)
observe exam(cachexia)
observe labs(elevated_inflammatory_markers)

% --- imaging ---
observe imaging(small_bowel_wall_thickening)
observe imaging(mesenteric_lymphadenopathy)
observe imaging(diffuse_small_intestine_hypermetabolism)
observe imaging(asymmetric_sacroiliitis)

% ===== QUERIES =====
% q1/q2/q4 — unifying diagnosis / cause of the malabsorptive enteropathy
? diagnosis(whipple_disease)
? diagnosis(small_bowel_lymphoma)
? diagnosis(coeliac_disease)
? diagnosis(crohn_enteropathy)
? diagnosis(intestinal_tuberculosis)

% q3 — recommended next step
